; BOUNCE BONANZA - song 5, course 5: "Summit Rush" (SPEC.md 128.20)
;
; E minor at 164 BPM - a 16th is one row of FIVE sub-ticks (91.6 ms), straight.
; A pattern is ONE bar (rows 16), not two: the bass, the stabs and the drums
; are a bar per chord, so every Em, C, D and B bar shares one phrase and the
; song stays small for its length.
;
; The intro is the engine: a bar of the E bass pumping alone under the beat,
; then a fanfare up a B major chord. A is the hook on the trumpet - B up to
; E up to B, then a tumble down to E - answered a step lower over D, over
; Em C D B, Em C Am-B Em, with off-beat-pushed stabs (3+3+2) and a rock beat.
; B LIFTS to G major on the horn: broad held notes with eighth pickups over a
; string pad, G D Em C G D C D. C is the climb, on the chip: the hook's own
; leap shape (a fifth below the root, the root, the third) on C, then D, then
; Em, twice - the second pass an octave up - and a B major arpeggio and a
; tom fill throw it back into the hook. Intro, A B C for ever: 24 bars.
;
; The SPEAKER hears the lead whole - every rest in it is filled by the bass
; (`spkbass`) - with the kick and snare blipping the beats; hats are silent
; there. The arpeggiated notes (chiparp, chiparpm) arpeggiate on both arms.

song summit "Summit Rush"
groove 5
unit 16
rows 16
measure 16
spkbass
voice lead trumpet
voice bass pluckbass
voice chord stab

; --- the band: a bar per chord, shared by every section -------------------------
bass BE = o2 l8 e e >e <e e e >e <e |
bass BC = o2 l8 c c >c <c c c >c <c |
bass BD = o2 l8 d d >d <d d d >d <d |
bass BB = o1 l8 b b >b <b b b >b <b |
bass BG = o2 l8 g g >g <g g g >g <g |
bass BAB = o1 l8 a a >a <a b b >b <b |
chord CEm = o4 v10 [e g b]4. [e g b]4. [e g b]4 |
chord CC = o4 v10 [e g >c]4. [e g >c]4. [e g >c]4 |
chord CD = o4 v10 [f+ a >d]4. [f+ a >d]4. [f+ a >d]4 |
chord CB = o4 v10 [d+ f+ b]4. [d+ f+ b]4. [d+ f+ b]4 |
chord CAB = o4 v10 [e a >c]4 [e a >c]4 [d+ f+ b]4 [d+ f+ b]4 |
chord SG = @strings o4 v10 [d g b]1 |
chord SD = @strings o4 v10 [f+ a >d]1 |
chord SEm = @strings o4 v10 [e g b]1 |
chord SC = @strings o4 v10 [e g >c]1 |
drum DR = k8 h8 s8 h8 k8 k8 s8 h8 |
drum DB = k8 h8 s8 h8 k8 h8 s8 h8 |
drum DF = k8 h8 s8 h8 k8 s8 T16 T16 t16 t16 |
drum DF2 = k8 h8 s8 h8 s16 s16 T16 T16 T16 t16 t16 t16 |

; --- the intro: the bass alone, then the fanfare ----------------------------------
lead LI = v14 o4 f+8 f+8 b8 >d+8 f+4 @chiparp <b4 |

; --- A: the hook, Em C D B / Em C Am-B Em --------------------------------------------
lead LA1 = v14 o4 b8 >e8 b8 a16 g16 f+8 g8 e4 |
lead LA2 = v14 o6 c4. <b8 g4 e4 |
lead LA3 = v14 o4 a8 >d8 a8 g16 f+16 e8 f+8 d4 |
lead LA4 = v14 o5 f+4. g8 f+4 d+4 |
lead LA7 = v14 o6 c8 <b8 a8 e8 d+8 f+8 a8 f+8 |
lead LA8 = v14 o5 g8 f+8 @chiparpm e2 r4 |

; --- B: the lift to G major, on the horn ---------------------------------------------
lead LB1 = @horn v13 o5 r8 d8 g8 a8 b2 |
lead LB2 = @horn v13 o5 a8 b8 a8 f+8 @chiparp d2 |
lead LB3 = @horn v13 o5 r8 e8 g8 a8 b2 |
lead LB4 = @horn v13 o6 c4. <b8 a8 g8 e4 |
lead LB5 = @horn v13 o5 r8 d8 g8 a8 b4. >d8 |
lead LB6 = @horn v13 o6 f+4. e8 d2 |
lead LB7 = @horn v13 o6 e4. d8 c4 e4 |
lead LB8 = @horn v13 o6 d4. c8 <a4 f+8 d8 |

; --- C: the climb, C D Em twice, on the chip ------------------------------------------
lead LC1 = @chip v13 o4 g8 >c8 e4. d8 c4 |
lead LC2 = @chip v13 o4 a8 >d8 f+4. e8 d4 |
lead LC3 = @chip v13 o4 b8 >e8 g4. f+8 e4 |
lead LC4 = @chiparpm v13 o5 e2 @chip <b8 >d8 e8 f+8 |
lead LC5 = @chip v13 o5 g8 >c8 e4. d8 c4 |
lead LC6 = @chip v13 o5 a8 >d8 f+4. e8 d4 |
lead LC7 = @chip v13 o5 b8 >e8 g4. f+8 e4 |
lead LC8 = @chiparp v13 o5 b2 @chip a8 f+8 d+8 r8 |

order -   BE  CEm DR
order LI  BB  CB  DF
order LA1 BE  CEm DR          ; 2: the loop comes back here
order LA2 BC  CC  DR
order LA3 BD  CD  DR
order LA4 BB  CB  DR
order LA1 BE  CEm DR
order LA2 BC  CC  DR
order LA7 BAB CAB DR
order LA8 BE  CEm DF
order LB1 BG  SG  DB
order LB2 BD  SD  DB
order LB3 BE  SEm DB
order LB4 BC  SC  DB
order LB5 BG  SG  DB
order LB6 BD  SD  DB
order LB7 BC  SC  DB
order LB8 BD  SD  DF
order LC1 BC  CC  DR
order LC2 BD  CD  DR
order LC3 BE  CEm DR
order LC4 BE  CEm DF
order LC5 BC  CC  DR
order LC6 BD  CD  DR
order LC7 BE  CEm DR
order LC8 BB  CB  DF2
loop 2
